 PERFORM public.update_recipe(v.id,v.slug,v.title,v.excerpt,v.ingredients,$s1$[{"title":"Prepare the whole chicken and deboning tools","content":"Start with a whole raw skin-on chicken, its legs and wings attached. Set out a non-slip board, sharp narrow boning knife, kitchen shears, large food-safe needle and twine, roasting rack, pan and food thermometer. Remove giblets, refrigerate the chicken and do not wash it. Preheat the oven to 180 °C shortly before roasting. If unsure, ask a butcher to remove only the bones described in steps 2 and 3.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Prepare the whole chicken and deboning tools","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-01.webp"},{"title":"Remove the body carcass without splitting the chicken open","content":"Work carefully through the rear cavity. Using short strokes along the bone, separate flesh from ribs, spine and breastbone without cutting through the skin or opening the back into a sheet. Release the body bones at the shoulder and hip joints while keeping both wings and legs attached. Remove the carcass and any loose bone fragments. Carefully remove proximal wing bones if present while keeping the wing tips and their bones in place.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Remove the body carcass without splitting the chicken open","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-02.webp"},{"title":"Remove ONLY the upper thigh bones, not the lower drumstick bones","content":"From inside the joint between each leg and body, locate the upper thigh bone (femur). Work the meat away from it without piercing skin, release it at the hip and knee joint, and slide it out. Repeat on the other side. Keep the bone inside each LOWER drumstick and the bones in the wing tips. You now have two empty upper thigh pockets to fill; keep their access openings for stitching and check for bone splinters.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Remove ONLY the upper thigh bones, not the lower drumstick bones","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-03.webp"},{"title":"Prepare vegetables, raisins and optional peas","content":"Parboil 100 g diced carrot until just tender, drain and cool. Cook and drain 100 g peas if using. Soak 90 g raisins in warm water for 10 minutes and drain. Soften 100 g onion and 80 g red pepper in 10 g oil for 5 minutes, then add 12 g garlic for 30 seconds. Cool completely before combining with raw meat.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Prepare vegetables, raisins and optional peas","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-04.webp"},{"title":"Combine the beef, pork, crumbs and raisins","content":"Mix 300 g ground beef, 300 g ground pork, 80 g plain breadcrumbs and one beaten large egg (50 g). Fold in the drained raisins, cooled vegetables, optional peas, 12 g parsley and half the salt, pepper, cumin and paprika. Do not overwork or warm the raw stuffing. Keep it refrigerated and prevent cross-contamination.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Combine the beef, pork, crumbs and raisins","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-05.webp"},{"title":"Fill and stitch BOTH deboned upper thighs","content":"Spoon stuffing into both empty upper thigh pockets, filling the spaces formerly occupied by the femurs but not forcing filling down the still-boned drumsticks. Shape the thighs gently so they retain their natural appearance. With food-safe needle and twine, stitch the small access openings toward the lower legs, and any cuts used to remove the thigh bones. Keep legs attached to the bird.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Fill and stitch BOTH deboned upper thighs","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-06-v2.webp"},{"title":"Fill the rear body cavity and sew it shut","content":"Place the remaining mixture inside the body through the rear opening, distributing it evenly without packing tightly enough to split the skin. Stitch the neck opening if it remains open, then sew the rear cavity securely. Check the openings at both upper thighs are also stitched. Cook any excess stuffing separately until its centre reaches at least 74 °C; never force it into the bird.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Fill the rear body cavity and sew it shut","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-07-v2.webp"},{"title":"Truss the legs and wings and roast the WHOLE bird","content":"Keep the lower drumstick bones and wing-tip bones in place. Gently secure the wings at the sides and legs in their natural position. Mix the remaining 10 g oil with the other half of the salt, pepper, cumin and paprika, then brush over the skin. Roast breast-side up on a rack in the same pan at 180 °C for roughly 105–150 minutes, adjusting for the size of the bird and density of the stuffing. Tent loosely with foil if it browns too early. Oven time alone is not a safety test.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Truss the legs and wings and roast the WHOLE bird","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-08.webp"},{"title":"Check 74 °C in the breast, centre and BOTH thigh fillings","content":"Use a clean food thermometer to check the thickest chicken breast, the centre of the filling in the body, and the centre of each of the two stuffed upper thighs. Avoid touching the retained bones in the lower drumsticks and wing tips. Chicken and EVERY pocket of stuffing must reach at least 74 °C. If any point is cooler, keep roasting and recheck.","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Check 74 °C in the breast, centre and BOTH thigh fillings","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-09.webp"},{"title":"Rest and carve neat crosswise slices","content":"Rest the entire bird for 15 minutes with legs and wings still attached. Carefully remove ALL stitches from the rear cavity, neck and upper thigh openings, plus trussing strings. Bone-in drumsticks and wing tips remain recognizable pieces; remove them when carving if they obstruct the knife. Cut the body crosswise into even 2–3 cm slices, not lengthwise. Neatly fan the slices beside the bird without spilling the compact beef-and-pork, raisin and vegetable stuffing. Refrigerate leftovers within 2 hours (within 1 hour above 32 °C).","image_alt":"Colombian Christmas stuffed chicken with beef and pork — Rest and carve neat crosswise slices","image_url":"https://manualdecocina.com/recetas/pollo-relleno-navideno/paso-10.webp"}]$s1$::jsonb,v.category,v.prep_time_minutes,v.cook_time_minutes,v.servings,v.image_url,true);
 n:=n+1;
